KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12 --unwind 4
^pointer handling for concurrency is unsound$
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
no body for callee
^warning: ignoring
--
The models of the standard library's thread start (libstdc++'s
_M_start_thread, libc++'s inline pthread_create) and join (both libraries)
start a second thread: symbolic execution reaches it and stops with
"pointer handling for concurrency is unsound" (issue #305), as for any C++
program with two threads whose library code writes a shared pointer.
With libc++ the thread was started before (its header calls
pthread_create); join, defined in libc++'s library, is modelled now.  When #305
is fixed, this test should expect the two assertions' results instead
(cpp11_probe_std_thread).
